---
title: "get_price_no_older_than (Pyth Sui Price Feeds: Use Real-Time Data)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_read_price: price_info = read_price_info(price_info_object)
    q_read_price --> q_get_timestamp: current_time = clock.timestamp_ms / 1000
    q_get_timestamp --> q_check_age: age = current_time - price.timestamp
    q_check_age --> q_return: age <= max_age
    q_check_age --> q_abort: age > max_age
    q_abort --> [*]: abort (price too stale)
    q_return --> [*]: return price_struct

    note right of q_check_age
        INV-001: price age must be <= max_age seconds (staleness guard)
        INV-002: current_time derived from Sui Clock object (on-chain time)
        INV-003: If price is stale, transaction aborts (no fallback)
    end note

    note right of q_read_price
        INV-004: PriceInfoObject must exist on-chain and be accessible
    end note
